prb@chinet.chi.il.us (Paul Botts) writes (regarding needs for difficult
monsters once a character attains experience level 10 or so)
>...
>put in monsters that are simply enemy characters. Valkyries, wizards, tourists,
>the whole lot of them. Only, they are outfitted just like you are, and
>_they use the wands and spellbooks same as you_!
>...
>I know just enough about programming (not much) to understand that this
>would be a real bear to code, especially if the creatures are to be at
>least a little "smart" about their behaviour, and I think that is what
>would make it worthwhile....

This is a great idea!  There is already code in place to handle ghost
characters, as well as a duplicate of the character called "player" that
I understand will sometimes appear.  The problem with these monsters is
that they don't have any special skills.  The "player" has a duplicate of
your weapons, armor, hit points... other than throwing and hitting with
wielded weapon, it doesn't have any special hits (wands, spells, etc.).
The ghosts are limited to "touch" attacks.  The only thing to add would
be special hits for different character classes, and some fairly cute
#chat code.
